 75NI c  1998Am04 (also 1995AmZY,1992WeZX): {+75}Ni identified after the        
 75NI2c  {+9}Be({+86}Kr,X) reaction at E=500 MeV/nucleon with a 2 g/cm{+2}      
 75NI3c  target. B|r-|DE-tof technique used, |b particles detected.             
 75NI c  2010Ho12 (also 2005Ho08): {+75}Ni identified in the {+9}Be({+86}Kr,X)  
 75NI2c  reaction at E=140 MeV/nucleon with a 376 g/cm{+2} target.              
 75NI2c  Fully-ionized {+86}Kr beam, A1900 fragment separator at NSCL facility  
 75NI3c  using B|r-|DE-B|r method. After separation, the mixed beam was         
 75NI4c  implanted into the NSCL |b-counting system (BCS) consisting of stacks  
 75NI5c  of Si PIN detectors, a double-sided Si strip detector (DSSD) for       
 75NI6c  implantation of ions, and six single-sided Si strip detectors (SSSD)   
 75NI7c  followed by two Si PIN diodes. The identification of each implanted    
 75NI8c  event was made from energy loss, time-of-flight information and        
 75NI9c  magnetic rigidity. The implantation detector measured time and         
 75NIac  position of ion implantations and |b decays. Neutrons were detected    
 75NIbc  with NERO detector. Measured |b- and |bn-correlated events with ion    
 75NIcc  implants, half-life of {+75}Ni and delayed-neutron emission            
 75NIdc  probability. A total of 1905 implants were detected, and 43            
 75NIec  correlated |bn coincidences were observed.                             
 75NI c  Theoretical calculations (half-life, %|b{+-}n): 1989Kr02, 2002Gr16,    
 75NI2c  2005Gr29, 2005Bo19, 2008Ma17.                                          
